  "live_records": {
    "q-341475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341475",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x>0.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{x})] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt[4]{x}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{2}}}]\\cdot {(\\sqrt[4]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[4]{x}\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1+\\sqrt{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
