    "q-95517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95517",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}+(-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{4})^{2}}})\\cdot ({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{8}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
