    "q-95519": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95519",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}+(-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+1|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}})\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+1)\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}(1-\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
