    "q-341460": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341460",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-4\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|}$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-4\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(3-2x)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|\\sqrt{1+(3-2x)^{2}}}]\\cdot (3-2x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{|3-2x|\\sqrt{1+(9-12x+4{x}^{2})}}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|3-2x|}\\,\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{10-12x+4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
