    "q-95523": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95523",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\sqrt{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1-x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
