    "q-313240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q313240",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(2\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(5x)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
