    "q-95528": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95528",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}})\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{ln}^{2}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
