    "q-341516": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341516",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({3}^{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({3}^{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{({3}^{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot {({3}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{9}^{x}}}\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\sqrt{1-{9}^{x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
