    "q-341535": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341535",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[3\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-{(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt[3]{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2/3}}\\frac{1}{(1-\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
