    "q-95544": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95544",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y={e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{-x})^{′} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}-\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{-2x}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}-{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{-2x}}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
