    "q-341524": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341524",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(-x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(-x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1-(-x)^{2}}\\cdot (-x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
