    "q-95558": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95558",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95558-a",
